677
00:40:03,361 --> 00:40:06,360
that defy description.

678
00:40:06,361 --> 00:40:11,360
But what does the future hold for this ever-evolving treat?

679
00:40:11,361 --> 00:40:14,360
One company claims to already have the answer.

680
00:40:14,361 --> 00:40:17,360
The same way that a microwave oven

681
00:40:17,361 --> 00:40:19,360
reinvented the way that people cooked their food

682
00:40:19,361 --> 00:40:24,360
we've somewhat reinvented the way that people think of ice cream.

683
00:40:24,460 --> 00:40:27,360
This is Dippin' Dots, the self-proclaimed

684
00:40:27,460 --> 00:40:29,860
ice cream of the future.

685
00:40:29,960 --> 00:40:33,100
Here in this nondescript Paducah, Kentucky plant,

686
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:37,120
folks are churning out a unique product.

687
00:40:37,220 --> 00:40:39,420
Unique because of its beaded shape,

688
00:40:39,520 --> 00:40:42,360
but also because it's been frozen cryogenically

689
00:40:42,460 --> 00:40:43,360
using liquid nitrogen.

690
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:49,360
The process was the brainchild of microbiology

691
00:40:49,361 --> 00:40:52,960
and biologist Kurt Jones.

692
00:40:53,060 --> 00:40:55,600
I had been working on a project at work

693
00:40:55,700 --> 00:40:57,360
where we were freezing yogurt cultures,

694
00:40:57,460 --> 00:40:59,800
and I had developed a way to do it using liquid nitrogen,

695
00:40:59,900 --> 00:41:02,200
which is 320 below zero.

696
00:41:02,300 --> 00:41:04,500
It just made me think, I wonder if I could freeze ice cream

697
00:41:04,600 --> 00:41:08,620
in the same way, and how it would react.

698
00:41:08,720 --> 00:41:13,120
Kurt soon had his answer, and the result is Dippin' Dots.

699
00:41:13,220 --> 00:41:15,420
It all begins with a standard pasteurized mix

700
00:41:15,520 --> 00:41:19,120
that is flavored with one of Dippin' Dots' 30 flavors.

701
00:41:19,121 --> 00:41:22,460
That's when the fun begins.

702
00:41:22,461 --> 00:41:25,120
Once we've completed the flavoring process,

703
00:41:25,121 --> 00:41:28,000
the product is then transferred to what you see behind me,

704
00:41:28,001 --> 00:41:29,840
a cryogenic processor.

705
00:41:29,841 --> 00:41:31,420
In the top of the processor, there's

706
00:41:31,421 --> 00:41:34,340
an instrument that allows a measured amount of mix

707
00:41:34,341 --> 00:41:36,880
to come into contact with liquid nitrogen,

708
00:41:36,881 --> 00:41:38,260
and then it freezes instantly.

709
00:41:41,020 --> 00:41:43,060
That instrument at the top of the processor

710
00:41:43,061 --> 00:41:45,820
functions like an eyedropper, releasing the mix

711
00:41:45,821 --> 00:41:48,300
in tiny droplets.

712
00:41:48,301 --> 00:41:50,760
When the droplets hit the liquid nitrogen,

713
00:41:50,761 --> 00:41:55,260
they're flash frozen into beads that descend like BBs.

714
00:41:55,261 --> 00:41:58,260
An inclined auger releases a gallon of beads into each bag.

715
00:42:01,620 --> 00:42:03,880
Due to this radical freezing technique,

716
00:42:03,881 --> 00:42:06,700
the beads contain only the tiniest ice crystals

717
00:42:06,701 --> 00:42:08,840
and almost no air.

718
00:42:08,841 --> 00:42:11,520
They're also a lot colder than regular ice cream,

719
00:42:11,521 --> 00:42:15,080
coming in at minus 20 degrees.

720
00:42:15,081 --> 00:42:16,980
Scientifically speaking, it gives it

721
00:42:16,981 --> 00:42:19,080
a very, very creamy, smooth taste,

722
00:42:19,081 --> 00:42:23,980
even though it's a real fun and novel product.

723
00:42:23,981 --> 00:42:25,880
The beads are immediately packed into bags

724
00:42:25,881 --> 00:42:28,360
to be shipped worldwide.

725
00:42:28,361 --> 00:42:30,300
To maintain their creaminess, they're stored

726
00:42:30,301 --> 00:42:34,660
in the subarctic minus 50 degree freezer.

727
00:42:34,661 --> 00:42:36,360
There's lots of times we like to tell everybody

728
00:42:36,361 --> 00:42:39,160
it's the largest, coldest freezer in America,

729
00:42:39,161 --> 00:42:41,700
because at that temperature, it stores more product

730
00:42:41,701 --> 00:42:45,580
than any product like that in the US.

731
00:42:45,581 --> 00:42:49,820
In 2007 alone, Dippin' Dots sold more than 2 million gallons

732
00:42:49,920 --> 00:42:51,720
of the chili beads.

733
00:42:51,820 --> 00:42:54,020
You'd have to have Brain Freeze discovered those numbers.

734
00:42:57,020 --> 00:43:00,420
The future also looks bright for another innovative ice cream,

735
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:04,640
slow churn, first developed at Dryer's.

736
00:43:04,740 --> 00:43:07,940
And we spent $20 million, 15 years,

737
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:10,980
in developing what is called slow churn,

738
00:43:11,080 --> 00:43:13,340
which is not added ingredients.

739
00:43:13,440 --> 00:43:14,940
It's a process.

740
00:43:14,941 --> 00:43:19,080
And this process takes the temperature down

741
00:43:19,081 --> 00:43:21,780
and we freeze it much colder.

742
00:43:21,781 --> 00:43:25,960
And by doing so, you have a real fine texture

743
00:43:25,961 --> 00:43:29,020
that gives you creaminess with great appearance

744
00:43:29,021 --> 00:43:30,180
and great flavor.

745
00:43:31,720 --> 00:43:33,120
